  "text": {
    "tagline": "Instruments of the cloister and the market square.",
    "blurb": "The second volume of the Collegium Series gathers {count} instruments from the chapel and the courtyard: Flemish harpsichords, folk harp, psaltery, strumstick and dan tranh beside kalimbas, mbira, balafon, hand chimes, tubular bells and gong.",
    "intro": [
      "Welcome to Courtyard & Chapel, the second volume of the Cantiga Collegium Series. Where the first volume stayed indoors, this one opens the doors: the instruments of the chapel stand beside those of the market square, as they did in many a town.",
      "You will find keyboards and plucked strings, mallets and bells, and a few sound effects from the square. The programme notes in NOTES.PDF describe each one."
    ],
    "maker_note": [
      "Our members asked for instruments they could not keep at home: a harpsichord tuned for the season, a gong, a balafon. We hope this disc brings them into the study.",
      "dr. Anneke van Leeuwen, for the Cantiga Early Music Press"
    ],
    "install": [
      "Insert the disc. In the Library tab it appears as COURTYARD.",
      "Open a folder and double-click a preset to load it.",
      "The programme notes are NOTES.PDF; the sound credits are in CREDITS.TXT."
    ],
    "license": [
      "CANTIGA EARLY MUSIC PRESS - LICENCE",
      "You may use the presets on one computer and perform and record music made with them freely.",
      "The recordings on this disc are public domain or CC0 (see CREDITS.TXT). The presets, notes and artwork are the Press's.",
      "No warranty."
    ],
